oh my god i feel like nicole kidman and  moulin rouge  everyone is talking about netflix's  emily in paris  love it or hate it this show has become  our latest obsession  are you looking for more emily in paris  after binging the whole season  well you've come to the right place  we've got all the behind the scenes  tidbits to get you through your emily  and paris withdrawal  from filming secrets you didn't know  about to memorable off-screen moments  between the cast  you'll love this peek at what went on  behind the scenes of this netflix hit  this is a very important shoot i'm just  going to be getting some behind the  scenes for social in the states  the look that emily rocks to the opera  is an homage to audrey hepburn  emily looks stunning in this christian  soriano dress  that she wears to the palace garnier  opera house in episode 6.  the look was a deliberate homage to  audrey hepburn in funny face  in which she gracefully walks down the  very same steps of the garnier opera  that emily does it helps that lily  collins is a dead ringer for audrey and  she definitely embodies the glamour that  audrey hepburn lived  and breathed the crew had the opera  house all to themselves for filming  which makes this moment  extra special there were so many camera  angles and camera shots to get within  the scene to kind of amplify the beauty  of the location  remember the dress emily wears you know  the dress  the gorgeous white gown she models at  the designer auction in episode nine  only for it to get art attacked by paint  well lily collins actually got to keep  the iconic dress  the dress was designed by french fashion  designer stephanie roland who actually  designed all the beautiful dresses in  the designer showroom  after they filmed the show roland sent  lily a clean version of the dress to  keep  we're more than a little jealous this  was the most important for me  to bring lightness to women we all know  that emily in paris takes place in  well paris duh it's right there in the  title but did you know that the entire  show was  actually shot on location in paris and  the nearby loire valley  according to lily collins it's also the  first american show that's completely  shot in paris  so all those iconic landmarks you see  the characters hanging around  are the real deal we love the show's  commitment to shooting where it's  actually set  for me the luckiest thing about shooting  there was the access to the incredible  locations that we got  it adds a dose of authenticity that  can't be replicated  and turns the show into a true love  letter to the city of paris  paris seems like a big city but it's  really just a small town  unlike emily who doesn't speak a lick of  french and relies on an app to translate  for her  lily collins was practically fluent in  french growing up she would read speak  and even dream in french but she stopped  practicing years ago  and lost much of the language but being  back in paris for the show had her  dreaming in french again  despite her character being hopelessly  bad at it lily even said play a  character that  hardly understands the language at all  it was very difficult for me  and then switch into totally speaking  french creator darren starr wanted his  writer's room to have the same  experience  emily goes through as a fish out of  water seeing paris for the first time  to ground the show in lived reality so  he sent his writers to live in and  experience the city first hand  it must have been quite the treat for  those who had never been and even though  the storyline had been planned out ahead  much of the actual writing for the  series happened on the ground when they  were in paris  getting cast on emily in paris must have  been a dream for star lily collins but  it also coincided with the opportunity  to work with director david fincher on  his upcoming netflix film  mank collins flew back and forth between  paris and los  angeles to attend mank rehearsals  juggling both projects at the same time  that meant that on a couple of occasions  she had to fly back to la  on the weekend for a 24-hour period and  then immediately fly back and go  straight to set for emily  as she put it i was in the air longer  than i was on the ground during those  crazy weekends anyway it's not just  about the number of followers  it's about content emily's amazing phone  case that looks like an old-school  camera belonged to costume designer  patricia field  she picked it up on a trip to korea lily  collins loved it and  insisted on making it a part of the  character who loves all things fashion  and photography  you know we are all a little afraid of  you  what it ended up being an identifying  character piece  similar to carrie bradshaw's necklace  creator darren starr wasn't totally into  the idea at first but field knew it  would work  she was right the phone case is super  chic and we'd love to know where we can  find one for ourselves  even when you're very hungry  in fact a number of pieces in emily's  wardrobe came from patricia field's  personal closet  field who is known for her amazing work  on sex than the city and the devil wears  prada didn't like some of the wardrobe  choices available to her so she simply  let lilly collins use some of her own  personal clothing items  in particular she lent her mcm backpack  and hood by air jacket to the character  when you have items this fashionable why  not use them we think it's cool patricia  field got to lend such a personal touch  to emily's style  oh um can i get a big one like cashmere  darren starr the genius behind the show  also created sex in the city and carrie  bradshaw's influence on emily is  noticeable  star also worked closely with patricia  field on sex in the city  naturally they paid homage to the show  through outfits and design choices  in one episode for instance emily wears  a pair of earrings that spell her name  which is an homage to carrie bradshaw's  carry necklace  other little references are made through  some of emily's outfits like the black  tool skirt she wears that reminds us of  carrie's signature tutu  never mind sorry it's a long story lily  collins believes that emily herself took  a lot of inspiration from carrie  bradshaw  saying i think she took into  consideration if carrie went to france  what would she wear  what would she do on top of that we  can't help but think emily's experience  of coming to paris mirrors the time that  carrie visited paris in the final season  of sex in the city  right down to filming in the iconic  hotel plaza athene  where carrie bradshaw stayed in the  series finale there's no doubt emily had  carrie on her mind when she visited this  beautiful parisian building  i grew up loving saxon city love carrie  bradshaw  darren starr thinks he subconsciously  picked the name emily because he loved  how the french pronounce  emily emily  and of course we can't think of the name  emily without thinking of the film  emily which is about a native but  imaginative parisian girl named  emily both emily in paris and the film  emily  shared a romanticized but whimsical  approach to the city so we can't help  but think it played a part in choosing  the name  and speaking of names emily's friend  mindy was named after a real friend of  darren stars  who lives in paris you can't have a show  set in paris without a dreamy french  love interest  and boy does lucas bravo succeed in that  role as the hot chef gabriel  you're the chef here wait is there a  problem  according to darren starr bravo was put  through the ringer before landing the  role  having to come back and audition  multiple times it wasn't until he came  back and did an audition with lily  collins that the deal was sealed  their chemistry was too good to deny and  it  shows i'm gonna miss you so much and i  the cast hung out and went wine tasting  in between scenes shot in the loire  valley  lucas bravo mentions that between scenes  we went wine tasting because there was a  vineyard nearby  in general the cast got to shop and  whine and dine in and around paris  just like their characters we can't  blame them for taking advantage of being  in paris of all places  the amazing behind the scenes photos  that the cast has shared on social media  have us  itching to catch a plane straight to  paris and never leave  it's perfect it's perfect  we love when actors rub off on the  characters they play in tv shows  and get to influence the writing one  example is that mindy wasn't supposed to  be a singer until ashley park was cast  ashley park has an amazing voice which  she showed off as gretchen and mean  girls the musical  darren starr loved her and her voice so  much that he made it a part of mindy's  character  he says he selfishly just wanted to hear  her voice but we're all thankful for it  i guess i thought you wouldn't  understand bonding is inevitable when  you spend so much time together with  your cast mates on a once in a lifetime  experience like this one  and the emily in paris cast is no  exception the cast really bonded and  became best friends while shooting  and they've shared little tidbits from  the set on social media like these funny  faces lucas bravo makes  into the camera in between takes  secretly captured by ashley park  and even though lucas and ashley barely  have any scenes together  the two lived next to each other while  filming and became inseparable  it looks like the cast of emily and  paris had the time of their lives  shooting this show and how could they  not being immersed in the city of love  did you enjoy these behind the scenes  moments from netflix's latest hit  leave a comment below and don't forget  to subscribe for more awesome videos  a la prochaine
 

